-- Row il-71. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: the instruments, the instructions and printed texts the two items read, item I1 and item I2, and the commencements as the pages print them.
-- Tests of the controls are in sv71-tests-controls.l4, tests that pin the readings are in sv71-tests-readings.l4, and the assertions that FAIL on purpose (two, one per item) are in sv71-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY) by tools/srcquote.py; N is the line number in the whole page, which the excerpt's header lists.
-- `ext:[shNNN-pPPP]` lines quote the Hebrew printed on the deposited image of Sefer HaChukim (SH) issue NNN, printed page PPP (registers/source-bundle/pages/). They are official instruments.
-- Every Hebrew string typed below is a stretch of the ext: line above it, and tools/hebcheck.py checks that each Hebrew run of this module is in the excerpt or on an ext: line.
-- Where a quotation mark is printed around a term, the ext: line types it as the Hebrew gershayim; the consolidation prints a different pair of marks (NOTES.md, fork F3). The tests look for the term without marks.
-- Nothing is quoted from memory. Every date, number and section below is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md.

§ `References`

